\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces Validity-guided framework for artefact-level LLM measurement. The framework proceeds from theoretical specification of the object of claim $\eta (d_i)$ to LLM measurement operationalization and empirical evaluation. Construct specification selects a criterion set $C_m$ for representation $m$, where $m \in \{H,M,F\}$ indexes holistic, macro-formative, and fine-grained formative construct representations, respectively. The number of criteria in representation $m$ is denoted by $J_m = |C_m|$. For each artefact $d_i$ and criterion $c_j \in C_m$, the model input $\mathbf  {u}_{ijm}=[\,s\,;\,c_j\,;\,d_i\,]$ is passed to the LLM measurement operator, which returns a criterion-specific rating distribution $\mathbf  {p}_{ijm}$ over $L$ valid rating levels. The criterion-level distributions are stacked into $\mathbf  {P}_i(C_m)\in [0,1]^{J_m\times L}$, summarized using expected values $x^{\mathrm  {EV}}_{ijm}$ and entropy $H_{ijm}$, and evaluated through validity evidence and measurement diagnostics. These empirical evidence streams determine the permitted artefact-level claims addressed by RQ1 and RQ2. The informed holistic control used in the FeedbackQA analysis is omitted for simplicity, because it functions as a design control rather than as a separate construct-representation category.}}{30}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:measurement_framework}{{3}{30}{}{figure.3}{}}
